{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Instances.Real.Lemmas","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.leading_margin_pos_of_VD_ceiling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.leading_margin_pos_of_VD_ceiling","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/M1DescentDPPConvergence.lean#L116-L143","doc":"**The leading-margin field, reduced to the rigorous `V_D` ceiling (sorry-free).**\n\n`leading_margin_pos` asks `sigRatioInf < rhoInf` with `sigRatioInf = √(V_D/V_A)`, `rhoInf = 2√6/5`.\nBecause `π` cancels in the square, this is exactly `V_D < 64/(75π²)` — and that bound is proved\nrigorously (certified interval partial sum + explicit analytic tail majorant,\n`wlambda_covariance_epic_M1_VD_ceiling_rigorous.py`: `V_D < 0.0415975 < 0.0864607`). This lemma is the\nLean reduction: given `V_A = 8/(9π²)`, `sigRatioInf² = V_D/V_A`, `rhoInf² = 24/25`\n(`CSMarginCorrelationConstant.csMargin_rhoSq_eq`), `0 ≤ rhoInf`, and the ceiling `V_D < 64/(75π²)`,\nthe strict inequality follows by `π`-cancellation in the square. **Unlike the two `Tendsto` fields,\nthis one is NOT gated on the open bulk kernel rate** — it is a fact about the exact limit constants,\nnow discharged modulo the certified numeric ceiling.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] docs/audits/2026-08-29-covariance-kernel-M1-po72-leading-constants.md ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.m1_pos_eventually","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.m1_pos_eventually","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/M1DescentDPPConvergence.lean#L87-L114","doc":"**`M₁ > 0` holds eventually (sorry-free), from the cited convergence.**\n\nCombines `cs_margin_eventually` with the Cauchy–Schwarz core: with the Fulman split\n`M₁ = P − N`, `P = ρ_P σ_A σ_W`, the universal `N ≤ σ_D σ_W`, and `σ_W > 0`, the margin\n`σ_D/σ_A < ρ_P` (⇔ `σ_D < ρ_P σ_A` since `σ_A > 0`) forces `M₁ = σ_W(ρ_P σ_A − σ_D) + (σ_D σ_W − N) > 0`.\n(The algebra mirrors `YoungDiagramKernelCSMargin.m1_pos_of_cs_margin`; kept inline so the file stays\nMathlib-only for standalone verification.) The eventual-vs-all-`n` gap is closed by the explicit\nthreshold from [gorbunov2024] plus the exact table, via `…CSMargin.m1_pos_all_of_base_and_tail`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.cs_margin_eventually","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.cs_margin_eventually","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/M1DescentDPPConvergence.lean#L78-L85","doc":"**The (CS) margin holds eventually (sorry-free), from the cited convergence.**\n\nSince `σ_D/σ_A → sigRatioInf < rhoInf ← ρ_P`, eventually `σ_D(n)/σ_A(n) < ρ_P(n)`. This is the\n`hCS`-input of `YoungDiagramKernelCSMargin.m1_pos_of_cs_margin` for all large `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.DescentDPPMarginConvergence.leading_margin_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.DescentDPPMarginConvergence.leading_margin_pos","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/M1DescentDPPConvergence.lean#L76-L76","doc":"the leading margin is strictly positive. -- Ref: [leitner2026] docs/audits/2026-08-29-covariance-kernel-M1-po72-leading-constants.md ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.DescentDPPMarginConvergence.sigRatio_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.DescentDPPMarginConvergence.sigRatio_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/M1DescentDPPConvergence.lean#L74-L74","doc":"`σ_D(n)/σ_A(n) → √(V_D/V_A)`. The bulk rate is a Toeplitz-determinant Fisher–Hartwig asymptotic\n(arc symbol ⇒ algebraic remainder), the remaining open computation.\n-- Ref: [johansson2001] [gorbunov2024] [deift-its-krasovsky2012] ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.DescentDPPMarginConvergence.rhoP_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.DescentDPPMarginConvergence.rhoP_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/M1DescentDPPConvergence.lean#L70-L70","doc":"`ρ_P(n) → ρ_P∞`. -- Ref: [ivanov-olshanski2003] [borodin-okounkov-olshanski2000] ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.DescentDPPMarginConvergence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.DescentDPPMarginConvergence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/M1DescentDPPConvergence.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.DescentDPPMarginConvergence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M1DescentDPPConvergence.DescentDPPMarginConvergence","kind":"class","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/M1DescentDPPConvergence.lean#L54-L76","doc":"**Conditional class (cited external input): the descent-DPP (CS)-margin ingredients converge to\ntheir exact leading limits, with a strictly positive leading gap.**\n\nParameterized by the finite-n correlation `rhoP = Corr(Σ|c|, ω₃)(n)`, the finite-n ratio\n`sigRatio = σ_D(n)/σ_A(n)`, and their limits. The three fields carry genuine content:\n\n* `rhoP_tendsto` — `ρ_P(n) → ρ_P∞`.\n  Ref: [ivanov-olshanski2003] (limit) · [borodin-okounkov-olshanski2000] (descent DPP / bulk kernel).\n* `sigRatio_tendsto` — `σ_D(n)/σ_A(n) → √(V_D/V_A)`.\n  Ref: [johansson2001] (tail Lemma 3.9 + de-Poisson Lemma 3.8) · [gorbunov2024] (bulk rate machinery).\n* `leading_margin_pos` — `√(V_D/V_A) < 2√6/5`, i.e. `m∞ > 0`\n  (`CSMarginCorrelationConstant.csMargin_rho_eq`; `V_D < 64/(75π²)`).\n\nNo instance is provided: an instance would assert the open bulk-rate result. ","signatureChunk":0}]}